{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And Moses said to the people: Do not fear.</b> [Fear not] the hearing of the voice of HaShem — 'for in order to test you has Elohim come, and in order that His fear be upon your faces.' He said that it is good for you to receive the commandments through vision and hearing together, for from each one separately a unique purpose emerges. For regarding the hearing He gave a reason: 'in order to test you has Elohim come,' and 'test' (נַסּוֹת) is an expression of raising a banner (נֵס), for HaShem wished to elevate you with surpassing exaltation above all the peoples; therefore He wants you to hear His voice, for the like has never been heard in any nation, such that you would be able to boast of this — that you heard the voice of Elohim and lived, as it is written (Deuteronomy 5:23): ״כִּי מִי כָל בָּשָׂר אֲשֶׁר שָׁמַע קוֹל אֱלֹהִים חַיִּים מְדַבֵּר מִתּוֹךְ הָאֵשׁ כָּמֹנוּ וַיֶּחִי״. And from here is a clear and solid proof that the hearing of the voice of Elohim is for Israel the raising of a banner above every nation and tongue. And regarding the seeing of the letters before them in the air, He gave a second reason and said: 'in order that His fear be upon your faces, so that you do not sin' — for the Torah is called 'the fear of HaShem, pure' (תְּהוֹרָה), and this depiction the Holy One, blessed be He, wanted to be upon your faces always, so that it would forever appear to you as though the Torah were written before you, so that you would never come to sin, for it would never depart from your mouth by virtue of the fact that the traced outlines of these letters would remain before you always. And this is a very precious interpretation."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:21:58.708688749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}